   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The outermost operation is a product of \\( 3 x \\) and \\( e^{- x - 3} \\), so the product rule comes first; the second factor is a composite, so its derivative needs the chain rule with inner function \\( - x - 3 \\).",
         "rule_named": "classify the outermost operation"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "So \\( h'(x) = - 3 x e^{- x - 3} + 3 e^{- x - 3} \\).",
         "rule_named": "product rule, then chain rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At x = -1 the exponent is -2 and its derivative is -1, so \\( h'(-1) = \\frac{6}{e^{2}} \\).",
